 while a Republican-sponsored poll the same week showed an eleven-point lead.\n\nExpert ratings mostly call the race Likely Republican, with several at Lean Republican and one at Tossup. Prediction markets give Nez roughly a one-in-three chance of winning. A Democratic-friendly national environment and modest outside spending against Crane keep this from being a blowout, but the district's lean, the incumbency advantage and the money gap make Crane the clear favorite heading into November.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1703, "margin": -5.61}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2296, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2331, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2721, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1924, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2064, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2601, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2994, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2375, "margin": -5.0}]}